#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cathay army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$cathay.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structure and Discipline"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:128
msgid ""
"To reflect their empire’s high-quality military organisation and command "
"arrangements, Cathay commanders may issue orders to brigades of up to 6 "
"units instead of the usual 4. However, those 6-unit brigades must include at "
"least 2 units of Bannermen. The 6-unit brigade cannot include chariots, "
"cavalry, or Terracotta Warriors."
msgstr ""

#. 3: its, remove handguns,
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[handguns,†1]]1. Handguns"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:141
msgid ""
"Any or all of the army’s Crossbows units can be replaced by Handguns while "
"still counting for the Crossbow min/max value. Their projectiles can pierce "
"armour far easier than a crossbow bolt. Therefore, units hit by Handguns get "
"a −1 penalty for their armour rolls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[terracotta-warriors,†2]]2. Terracotta Warriors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:146
msgid ""
"These warriors are Undead, so cannot act on initiative, are unaffected by "
"terror or enemy within 20cm, and cannot be confused. They can only brigade "
"with themselves and give/receive support only to/from each other."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:149
msgid ""
"They can only be ordered by Sorcerers, who gain +1 command when doing so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[hu-cavalry,†3]]3. Hu Cavalry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:155
msgid ""
"They have a shooting range of 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can "
"draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, "
"including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line "
"of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[rocket-launcher,†4]]4. Rocket Launcher"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:163
msgid ""
"The Rocket Launcher is treated as a xref:rules:artillery-and-machines."
"adoc#stone-thrower[Stone Thrower] as described in the Rulebook, except it "
"shoots 1D6 times per phase and any hits inflicted have an armour save with a "
"−1 modifier. If the roll for the number of shots is 1, the Rocket Launcher "
"has misfired, and you must roll another D6 against the Rocket Launcher "
"Misfire Chart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rocket Launcher Misfire Chart"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|D6 |Result\n"
"\n"
"h|1\n"
"|*KABOOM!* The Rocket Launcher explodes in\n"
"spectacular manner.\n"
"\n"
"h|2–3\n"
"|*Dud.* The rocket does only one attack.\n"
"\n"
"h|4–5\n"
"|*Whoosh!* The rocket overshoots and does D6\n"
"attacks on the first unit in the line of fire\n"
"beyond the original target, regardless of range.\n"
"If the result is 1, don’t roll for the misfire\n"
"again. If the target is engaged in combat, the\n"
"hits are carried over into Combat phase. If\n"
"no target is behind the victim the rocket\n"
"leaves the battlefield without causing any\n"
"damage.\n"
"\n"
"h|6\n"
"|*Big badaboom!* The rocket does 2D6 attacks\n"
"instead of the normal 1D6.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:192
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[triple-bows,†5]]5. Triple Bows"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:194
msgid ""
"Triple Bows are xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#bolt-thrower[Bolt "
"Throwers] as described in the main rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:195
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[celestial-dragon,†6]]6. Celestial Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:199
msgid ""
"One Sorcerer per army can be upgraded to become a dragon which flies, gives "
"orders, casts spells, and causes terror. The dragon cannot give orders to "
"Terracotta Warriors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[tiger,†7]]7. Tiger"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:201
msgid "Tigers cannot be ridden by Sorcerers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[qilin,†8]]8. Qilin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:206
msgid ""
"Only a Sorcerer can ride a Qilin. Once per battle the Qilin’s magical power "
"adds +1 to the dice roll when casting a spell. The player must announce that "
"they are using the Qilin’s magic before rolling to see if the spell works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:211
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cathay spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "Glory of Cathay"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:221
msgid ""
"_Channelling powerful lores, the sorcerer gifts remarkable accuracy and "
"reloading dexterity to the empire’s defenders.  Their opponents are thereby "
"subjected to ferocious shooting._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:231
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon a friendly unit of unengaged missile-armed "
"infantry or chariots within range. The Sorcerer does not need to be able to "
"see the friendly unit nor their intended target.  When the spell is cast on "
"a unit, it can shoot twice that turn instead of once. If it has already shot "
"that turn it can therefore shoot again immediately. If it has yet to shoot "
"it can shoot twice.  When a unit shoots twice due to Glory of Cathay the "
"second shot is always at a minus 1 penalty and will therefore hit on a 5+."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lion Dogs Attack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:240
msgid ""
"_Complex astromancy allows the sorcerer to surround enemies with bright and "
"disorientating illusions in the form of terrible beasts._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:248
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any enemy unit within range regardless of whether "
"the Sorcerer can see it or not. The spell takes effect until the end of the "
"opposing player’s next turn. Whilst the spell lasts the unit cannot charge "
"and if engaged in combat will not pursue or advance. Even units that are "
"otherwise obliged to charge, pursue, or advance will not do so if affected "
"by this spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ferocity of Tigers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:258
msgid ""
"_Opening a portal to the past, the sorcerer imbues Cathay’s troops with the "
"spirit and stoicism of their ancestors. Filled with an overwhelming resolve "
"to protect the emperor, they surge forward to slay his foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:264
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on a friendly unit engaged in combat. The spell can "
"be cast regardless of whether the Sorcerer can see the target or not. The "
"spell lasts for the duration of the following combat phase. Every stand in "
"the unit adds +1 to its attacks value. The unit also becomes immune to "
"terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:266
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tranquility of Heaven"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:269
msgid "[.cost]#5+ to cast# [.points]#Range 15cm#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:273
msgid ""
"_Bestilling the sound and fury of battle, the sorcerer magically deadens the "
"fears of wavering soldiers, thus allowing the commands of their officers to "
"be faithfully obeyed._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/cathay.adoc:276
msgid ""
"All friendly units within 15cm of Sorcerer count as immune to terror until "
"the end of the enemy player’s next turn."
msgstr ""
